ZERO CONFLATED WITH ABSENT  
Line 33: input `r = {k: "0", robSummary: {high: 0, someConcerns: 0}}` makes `parseInt(r.k) || 0` indistinguishable from absent/invalid `k`. Consequence: a malformed or missing trial count is silently treated as real `k=0`.

ZERO CONFLATED WITH ABSENT  
Line 51: input `r = {k: "", or: 0}` makes `parseInt(r.k) || 0` collapse absent/invalid `k` to zero. Consequence: the clinical review reports a boundary condition instead of failing on missing data.

ZERO CONFLATED WITH ABSENT  
Line 75: input `r = {k: "abc", estimator: "DL"}` makes invalid `k` become zero. Consequence: the biostatistics warning is computed from fabricated `k=0`.

ZERO CONFLATED WITH ABSENT  
Line 48: input `benchmarks = [{lci: 0, uci: 1, citation: "X", measure: "OR", estimate: 0}]` suppresses no bug by itself, but `toFixed` requires numeric fields; input `{lci: "0", uci: "1", estimate: "0"}` reaches line 51 and throws. Consequence: string numeric benchmark data can break the review rather than produce findings.

STATUS CODE REPORTING THE WRAPPER rather than the work  
Line 194: input file containing an existing `/*PEER-REVIEW-v2*/` anywhere, plus a remaining `<script>/*PEER-REVIEW-v1*/...</script>`, returns `"SKIP: already-v2"`. Consequence: `main()` exits success while the intended conversion work was not done.

Idempotency guard satisfied by its OWN comment or marker rather than by the work  
Line 140: input HTML containing `<!-- /*PEER-REVIEW-v2*/ -->` and a real v1 script makes the converter skip. Consequence: a stray marker, not the completed replacement, satisfies idempotency.

Probe keyed to STRING A FIX REMOVES  
Line 143: after the first successful conversion removes all `PEER-REVIEW-v1` text, later runs cannot verify that the v2 script is correctly installed. Consequence: success removes the only conversion anchor.

